          <attvalue for="34" value="0.85" />
          <attvalue for="35" value="A surge in strikes against ports, rail hubs and shipping in the Black Sea and surrounding regions forces rerouting and longer transit times for container and bulk shipments, cascading into delays and higher transaction costs for North American firms that depend on tightly timed international inputs and thereby increasing US‑Canada cross‑border supply frictions." />
